  "name": "agg_object_vectors",
  "description": "Aggregations and update_by operators whose result is a vector of LocalDate, LocalTime, LocalDateTime, Duration, DayOfWeek or ZonedDateTime, of a table whose columns are vectors (group_by): min, max, median, percentile, unique, the formula aggregation's group (also of ZoneId), cumulative and rolling minimum and maximum, and the vectors inside a distinct or group of them (through an ungroup). Java's result column has the element type Object, which it sends as vectors of strings; Oxhaven sends LocalDate, LocalTime, Duration and ZonedDateTime elements typed, and the others as the same text (PARITY.md A27). Instants with fractions of 3, 6 and 9 digits, both DST changes of New York, before 1970, and nulls. Also a sort and an ungroup of such results, which Java sends as java.lang.Object. The aggregations that keep the element type (first, last, sorted_last) are left out: the server's test of recorded list fields does not know vectors of these classes.",
